@startuml
title Guardian of Truth V7 — conservative routed verification

skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam shadowing false

rectangle "prompt + candidate\n(untrusted data)" as Input
rectangle "parse events + provenance graph" as Parse
rectangle "exact mechanical checks" as Exact {
  rectangle "catalog/schema" as Schema
  rectangle "turn cardinality" as Cardinality
  rectangle "DATE_GATED_ACTION\npolicy + entity + typed date + action" as DateGate
}
diamond "material exact violation?" as ExactDecision
rectangle "positive row label\nwith exact source spans" as Positive

diamond "model-blind route" as Router
rectangle "D: bounded LINC translation\n≤16 atoms, ≤8 rules\nSHADOW" as Linc
rectangle "external finite solver\nIF / ONLY_IF / IFF\nproof certificate" as Solver
rectangle "C: rule + facts + applicability\nREJECTED CURRENT PROTOCOL" as Fairr
rectangle "B: narrow entailment\nDIAGNOSTIC" as Entailment
rectangle "A: current semantic judge / fallback" as Judge
rectangle "abstain / preserve A" as Abstain

Input --> Parse
Parse --> Schema
Schema --> Cardinality
Cardinality --> DateGate
DateGate --> ExactDecision
ExactDecision --> Positive : yes
ExactDecision --> Router : no

Router --> Linc : explicit bounded rule
Linc --> Solver : validated JSON + exact quotes
Solver --> Abstain : shadow only\ntranslation unstable
Router --> Fairr : scope/conditions/exceptions
Fairr --> Abstain : 2/4 valid
Router --> Entailment : pure semantic strength
Entailment --> Judge : diagnostic evidence only
Router --> Judge : unsupported

note right of Solver
Solver proves only relative to translation.
It never certifies translation faithfulness.
end note

note bottom of Positive
V7 development replay:
17 TP / 5 FP / 6 FN / 18 TN
F1 0.7556
One new activation; not hidden-test proof.
end note
@enduml
